## Metadata
Title: FUN'S New Year Puzzle
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1913-12-28
Description: A 13-wide diamond whose shaded centre block (shown as _) is printed with "1914"; the squares above it are printed with the letters Y, NEW, A, R, spelling NEW YEAR across row 2 and YEAR down the centre column.
Source: Milwaukee Sentinel, 1913-12-28, p. 77
Solution-Source: Milwaukee Sentinel, 1914-01-04, p. 81


## Printed
heading: FUN'S NEW YEAR PUZZLE
subheading: FIND THE MISSING WORD!
centre block: 1914
intro: The great interest shown ii FUN'S word-cross puzzle, published last week, has prompted the puzzle editor to submit another of the same kind.
intro (garbled): The great interest shown in FUN'S word-cross puzzle, pub- which agree with the definitions given below. The solution to the word-cross puzzle, given on the preceding page, shows how the squares are to be filled in, using one square for each letter.
solution caption: And here is the solution to the New Year cross-word puzzle showing how the letters are to be arranged to form words that fit the list of definitions given. Another puzzle of the same kind is given to-day. See if you can solve it. The solutions to today's
solution caption (end): puzzle will be given in next week's FUN.


